Small but important bug fix for CLI argument parsing.

```json
{
  "summary": "Fixed potential bug in CLI argument parsing where `args.indexOf('--limit') + 1` could cause undefined access when --limit flag is missing.",
  "learnings": [
    {"topic": "CLI parsing", "reminder": "Always check indexOf result !== -1 before using index+1 for array access"},
    {"topic": "Argument parsing", "reminder": "Store indexOf result in variable before doing arithmetic on it"}
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "critical",
      "file": "src/cli/index.ts (before fix)",
      "issue": "Original code: `args[args.indexOf('--limit') + 1]` - when --limit not found, this accesses args[1] which could be undefined or wrong value"
    }
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    "Consider using a CLI argument parsing library like yargs or minimist for more robust parsing"
  ],
  "praise": [
    "Good defensive programming - this fix prevents potential runtime errors",
    "Clean solution using early index storage"
  ],
  "overallScore": 92,
  "codeQualityScore": 90,
  "testCoverageScore": 95,
  "documentationScore": 95
}
```

